<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Privacy manifest. Required for App Store submission since spring 2024:
	  without it, an app that touches a "required reason" API fails validation
	  on upload — before TestFlight, not just before release.

	  Every entry below was derived by grepping the target, not by intent.

	  NSPrivacyTracking: false
	    No tracking of any kind. There is no AdSupport, no
	    AppTrackingTransparency, no attribution or analytics SDK, and no
	    third-party packages at all — the only `dependencies:` entry in
	    project.yml is the test bundle depending on the app.

	  NSPrivacyTrackingDomains: empty
	    There is no URLSession, URLRequest or NWConnection anywhere in the
	    target. The app makes no network calls. (PHImageRequestOptions
	    .isNetworkAccessAllowed is iOS fetching the user's own photo from their
	    own iCloud account through Apple's framework; nothing is uploaded and
	    there is no server on our side to upload to.)

	  NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes: empty
	    Nothing leaves the device, so nothing is "collected" in the sense this
	    key means. Photos are read via PHImageManager and analysed on-device by
	    Vision; feature prints and scores persist to a local SwiftData store.
	    Diagnostics reports are shared only when the user taps Share, and hold
	    counts, timings and memory figures — no photo content, no identifiers.

	  NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes: one entry, below.
	-->
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>

	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>

	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>

	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<!--
			  UserDefaults. Used in five places, all storing this app's own
			  settings under this app's own keys:
			    ScanScope        — the chosen scan window
			    TuningSettings   — on-device detection thresholds
			    ScanMetricsStore — the last diagnostics report + OOM marker
			    OnboardingView   — whether the welcome screen has been seen
			  No app group, no shared suite, nothing read back that this app did
			  not write. CA92.1 is exactly that case.
			-->
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>CA92.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
